WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.820
What do you think of when you hear the word&nbsp;
"vacation?" Perhaps you imagine lying by a beach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:11.340
watching the sunset over the clear blue&nbsp;
water, feeling the sand between your toes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:17.340
a tropical drink in your hand. Perhaps you see&nbsp;
yourself in a cozy log cabin in the woods, snow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:22.980
gently falling outside, a roaring fire warming&nbsp;
your feet while you catch up on your reading.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:29.220
Or maybe you think of a luxurious spa, seaweed&nbsp;
wraps, natural hot springs, and cucumber slices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:35.220
on your eyes. But what about those of us who are&nbsp;
sick of the usual getaways on offer, who want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:40.560
take a trip that not only shakes up their routine,&nbsp;
but their sense of reality as they once knew it?

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.540
Here at Marshall, Carter, and Dark, we strive&nbsp;
to provide vacation experiences for the more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:51.240
discerning traveler. The more, shall we&nbsp;
say, adventurous. Someone who's had enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.980
of those white sand beaches in the Caribbean,&nbsp;
who's sick of villas in the South of France,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.300
and wants to invest their hard-earned&nbsp;
money in a destination that is completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.820
and utterly unique. We've curated a selection&nbsp;
of potential vacation destinations to choose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:12.300
from for just that sort of customer, someone with&nbsp;
an adventurous spirit and money to burn. From the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:18.240
mind-bendingly surreal to the downright dangerous,&nbsp;
we promise that a trip to one of our prestige&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:24.900
vacation spots will help you make memories you&nbsp;
won't soon forget- no matter how hard you try.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:29.760
Most of our usual clientele wouldn't dream of&nbsp;
furnishing their home with items from an Ikea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:37.260
but don't let that stop you from considering the&nbsp;
first destination in our catalog! SCP-3008, also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:43.980
known as the Infinite Ikea, is less of a retail&nbsp;
store and more of an all-inclusive experience. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:50.100
looks like an ordinary Ikea from the outside, but&nbsp;
inside? Well, that's a different story altogether.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:54.420
Once you've passed through the main entrance&nbsp;
to the building, the possibilities are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.420 --> 00:02:00.720
literally endless, as the interior extends to an&nbsp;
infinite size defying all known laws of physics!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.340
You'll find a variety of accommodations,&nbsp;
from any furniture piece you can think of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:10.200
to a wide array of Scandinavian culinary&nbsp;
delights. Just watch out for the faceless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.740
entities in employee uniforms, and&nbsp;
don't let them catch you after dark!

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:19.200
Here's what Mary, 45, from Pennsylvania, had&nbsp;
to say about her stay in the Infinite Ikea:

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.460
"Please God, someone get me out of here! They took&nbsp;
my husband, and I'm getting so sick of meatballs!"

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:29.280
Are you something of a city slicker&nbsp;
looking for a country mouse experience?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.060
Trying to get away from all the hustle&nbsp;
and bustle and just kick back and relax,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.900
but also want to avoid going to the&nbsp;
same idyllic English villages that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:41.520
all your friends at the country club have&nbsp;
already tried? Look no further than Temby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.920
a charming little hamlet in Oxfordshire,&nbsp;
England, with its own specialized, local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:53.940
curse. You won't find this phenomenon anywhere&nbsp;
else, making for a truly exclusive experience.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:03:00.180
Every twelve years, an invisible entity known as&nbsp;
The Crooked Man spends 70 days targeting random&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:05.640
individuals in the town's limits, corrupting&nbsp;
the shape of their house, tormenting them with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:11.100
supernatural activity, and finally, twisting and&nbsp;
breaking their bones, stretching their limbs out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:16.140
beyond recognition. But don't worry, as a new&nbsp;
visitor to the town, it's unlikely you'd be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:20.880
picked. And even if you are, who doesn't like&nbsp;
coming home from a trip with a fresh new look?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.140
Here's what Jim, 32 from New York&nbsp;
City, thought of his time in Temby:

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:29.880
"You can't imagine the things I've heard...the&nbsp;
things I've seen... Have you ever seen a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:33.660
man whose legs bent in a dozen different&nbsp;
directions, so stretched out and deformed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:38.280
he can't even stand up anymore? I have. The&nbsp;
worst part was when the screaming stopped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:42.720
when he got used to the feeling of stretching&nbsp;
and cracking, bones snapping over, and over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.460
and over again until he was something else.&nbsp;
I hear that sound at night just before I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:52.200
fall asleep. I see him when I close&nbsp;
my eyes. I wish it had taken me too."

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:57.840
But maybe that isn't quite what you&nbsp;
have in mind. Maybe you're looking for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.700
more...permanent vacation. You've had quite&nbsp;
enough of the annoyances of everyday life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:06.960
of your neighbor's dog that just won't&nbsp;
stop barking at all hours of the night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.120
of the strangers standing too close to you in&nbsp;
line at Starbucks and breathing down your neck.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:17.940
You just want to leave it all behind for good, and&nbsp;
finally get some peace and quiet. If this sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:24.180
like you, then why not check out SCP-2935?&nbsp;
This space-time anomaly tucked away inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:29.460
of a limestone cave beneath a cemetery near&nbsp;
Joppa, Indiana contains the gateway to a world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:36.720
identical to our own, with one exception: Every&nbsp;
single life form there is dead. From the birds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:41.760
and the bees to the flowers and trees, to that&nbsp;
bartender that never makes your martini the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:47.940
you like it no matter how many times you explain&nbsp;
it to him, they're all gone. But keep in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:56.400
what happens in SCP-2935, stays in SCP-2935. By&nbsp;
which I mean, once you're there, you can't come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:01.860
back. Otherwise, death will follow you into&nbsp;
our world, and we can't have that now can we?

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:06.840
I'd provide you with a testimony from a&nbsp;
satisfied customer who stayed in SCP-2935,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:10.500
but every time I tried to get Eliza,&nbsp;
27, from Los Angeles on the phone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:14.760
it's all just static. So I guess&nbsp;
you'll have to take my word for it.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:19.320
Maybe you're not just looking for a vacation&nbsp;
to help you get away from it all. Perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:25.860
you're looking for a chance to self-reflect. Well,&nbsp;
there is no better place for that than SCP-1919,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:31.500
or the Hotel of Duplicates. It's an&nbsp;
early 20th-century hotel and converted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:36.900
mansion located at an undisclosed location -&nbsp;
address will be provided to you upon booking.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.600
On the outside, it's in mostly pristine condition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:45.780
but looks can be deceiving. The inside is&nbsp;
dilapidated and rotten, covered in water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:50.460
damage. When you enter the hotel, doppelgangers&nbsp;
of you will manifest throughout the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:56.700
looking exactly like you with a few notable&nbsp;
differences. Maybe they'll be missing their eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:02.700
or have unnaturally long arms or large jaws.&nbsp;
Whatever the case may be, all of these mirror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:08.520
images will become aggressive, attempting to&nbsp;
destroy you by any means necessary. You can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:13.260
either succumb to the attacks of your infinite&nbsp;
doubles, or somehow escape with your life.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:18.540
Talk about a way to get the blood pumping! And,&nbsp;
by coming face to face with yourself and your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:25.200
own flaws, you'll be able to leave the experience&nbsp;
with a new lease on life! If you survive, that is.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.260
Roberto, 55, from Indianapolis, had a great time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:31.500
at the Hotel of Duplicates!&nbsp;
Just listen to his testimony:

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:35.160
"No mirrors...please, cover the&nbsp;
mirrors. I can't look at it...can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.280
look at my face...there were so&nbsp;
many of them...so much blood..."

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:44.460
Up next is SCP-3001, or the Red Reality.&nbsp;
After so much time trapped in there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.400
Dr. Scranton needs some company! Just kidding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:52.920
of course. We may be ruled by the almighty&nbsp;
dollar, but we're not monsters. We'd never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:59.220
subject a paying customer to horrors of the&nbsp;
Red Reality. Speaking of red places, though…

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:06.480
Kick back poolside with SCP-354, the red pool!&nbsp;
You probably will want to swap out your swimsuit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:11.460
for a down coat, because it gets pretty cold up&nbsp;
in the wilderness of Northern Canada, but hey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:17.160
a pool is a pool! This pool is filled, not with&nbsp;
chlorinated water, but a thick red liquid similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:22.680
to human blood. Don't worry though, it's not&nbsp;
actually blood! That would be ridiculous.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:27.360
It's just a mysterious liquid of an unknown&nbsp;
origin, filling a pool that has no discernible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:33.060
bottom. Every so often, creatures will emerge from&nbsp;
the pool and attempt to attack anything they see.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:38.820
Who needs a trip to the zoo, when the animals&nbsp;
can come to you? You might encounter giant bats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:43.920
a levitating black sphere that emits directed&nbsp;
beams of radiation, an unknown abomination covered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:49.740
in tentacles, or something else you can't even&nbsp;
imagine! So pour a drink, kick off your shoes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:55.560
and maybe keep a weapon at the ready as you&nbsp;
lounge by the side of the picturesque red pool.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:08:00.300
Brandy, 24, from Chicago, had a&nbsp;
fantastic time at the red pool!

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:05.940
"This is Mochi, she's my cloud cat! Yeah, a cat&nbsp;
made out of water vapor. She came out of the pool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:10.380
and I gave her some tuna sashimi, and now she's&nbsp;
my best friend! Don't get too close though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.533
she's not into most humans, she'll&nbsp;
take your skin right off! Good kitty."

00:08:13.533 --> 00:08:19.260
Pip pip cheerio, jolly ol' London town,&nbsp;
innit? Have you always wanted to go to London,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:25.200
but find it just a bit too mainstream? Well, what&nbsp;
if there was a place you could visit that's just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:31.560
like London, but not quite? Well, I've got great&nbsp;
news for you, person with incredibly specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:40.140
tastes. SCP-1678, or UnLondon, is a full-scale&nbsp;
mirror image of London, located one kilometer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:45.660
beneath the city itself. It's a truly underground&nbsp;
spot. If you're a fan of the vintage look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:51.900
then that's even better! UnLondon is modeled after&nbsp;
the city as it appeared in the Victorian era, with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:57.180
gas lighting on the streets instead of electric,&nbsp;
and architecture reflecting that time period.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.860
UnLondon was constructed for human&nbsp;
habitation after an apocalyptic scenario,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:05.940
so make yourself comfortable! Take&nbsp;
a nap in a military-grade bunk bed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:09.780
wander around the Natural History&nbsp;
Museum's "Fall of Man" exhibit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:15.120
and savor a nice bowl of Dr. Goody’s Wonderfood!&nbsp;
Just be on the lookout for the Bobbies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:21.300
mechanized corpses fashioned into makeshift police&nbsp;
officers. They don't take kindly to trespassers!

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:25.260
But don't take my word for it,&nbsp;
listen to Chuck, 44, from Boston!

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:29.400
"UnLondon was wonderful. I love consuming&nbsp;
the nutrients found in Dr. Goody’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.720
Wonderfood, it provides me with everything my body&nbsp;
needs. I'm not frightened of the Bobbies anymore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:39.900
I'm a good citizen. I do not fear the Eyes in the&nbsp;
Sky and I do not pity the Wretches. They pay the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:44.640
price for their betrayals and will pay it the rest&nbsp;
of their days. The trip was worth the scurvy."

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:49.620
Sometimes you want to get out of civilization&nbsp;
and spend some time reconnecting with nature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:53.880
getting back to your roots. If you want to&nbsp;
go to a place where nobody knows your name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:59.520
and nobody should ever find out what&nbsp;
it is, then may I recommend SCP-4000?

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:04.680
I can't tell you too many details about it, you'll&nbsp;
have to see its unique charms for yourself, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:10.200
it's a forest that can be entered if you complete&nbsp;
the proper ritual, emerge from a well, and walk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:15.120
down a path to your destination. There are a&nbsp;
few strict rules you'll need to follow during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:20.220
your stay among the anomalous creatures that dwell&nbsp;
there: Don't call anything by a consistent name.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:27.180
Don't answer to a consistent name. Always accept&nbsp;
gifts, but do not consume them. And finally:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:32.640
if a ghost tells you it isn't a creature, obey&nbsp;
it. Don't let all the rules scare you though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:36.840
the beings in this enchanted forest&nbsp;
make for some really Good Neighbors.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:37.980
Just ask Barb-

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:42.960
"Shh! Don't say my name! Never say my name.&nbsp;
If you do, they'll take it. And once my name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:47.220
is gone...the rest of me follows. Don't&nbsp;
go into the forest, it's not worth it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:52.380
Don't dance with them, no matter how sweetly they&nbsp;
ask. And don't eat what they give you! Never,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:56.640
ever eat it. It's like the old poem&nbsp;
says, 'we must not look at goblin men,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:01.260
we must not buy their fruits, who knows upon&nbsp;
what soil they fed their hungry thirsty roots."

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:06.360
I know I said that these were all vacation spots,&nbsp;
but have you ever considered finding a new home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:12.900
instead? Somewhere you can put down roots and&nbsp;
really build a community? The people of SCP-599&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:18.480
are always looking for new neighbors, after&nbsp;
all. It's a small city located in an undisclosed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:23.880
location, earning it the nickname, Uncharted&nbsp;
City. Don't be dissuaded by the fact that everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:28.200
living in the town matches the description of&nbsp;
someone who went missing in a different, inferior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:34.200
town. This is a perfectly nice place to live,&nbsp;
and once you visit, you'll never want to leave.

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:36.720
Just ask Mario, 65, from Virginia!

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:40.920
"You really should think about purchasing&nbsp;
a house here, it's such a lovely place to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:45.480
raise a family. Just come and stay the night,&nbsp;
you'll see. This place was made for you."

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:50.460
Picture this, if you will: You're staying&nbsp;
the night in a luxurious Victorian mansion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:55.320
and it's a dark and stormy night. A clap&nbsp;
of thunder shakes you from your slumber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:59.580
and a flash of lightning illuminates the&nbsp;
bedroom where you sleep. Your heart leaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:03.840
into your throat as you think you see someone&nbsp;
standing at the foot of your bed. You light&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:09.000
a candle to check, but no. It's just a&nbsp;
chair with a coat slung over the back.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:16.500
You're alone. Just you, the enormous, empty house,&nbsp;
and the sound of rain pitter-pattering against the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:21.660
window. You can't relax, though, can't get your&nbsp;
mind to slip back into the blissful escape of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:26.400
sleep. You feel as if the walls are closing&nbsp;
in on you, as if the room is getting smaller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:30.780
and smaller, enveloping you in darkness. You&nbsp;
take your candle and use it to light the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:36.540
as you slowly open the door to the bedroom with&nbsp;
an eerie creek. Then, you step out into the hall.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:37.860
What was that sound?

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:43.680
That soft sigh, the padding of footsteps, coming&nbsp;
from over there. You turn, shining the flickering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:48.900
light of the flame in the direction of the noise,&nbsp;
and see the figure of a woman in a long, flowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:55.560
dress. She's beautiful, or she would be if she&nbsp;
looked alive. Instead, she's pale, translucent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.560 --> 00:13:01.860
her wide dark eyes staring into your very soul.&nbsp;
You can smell the scent of rotting plumeria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:08.160
flowers, the salt and iron of tears and blood.&nbsp;
Slowy, she begins to drift toward you. Not walk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:13.920
but float, as her feet never touch the ground.&nbsp;
You open your mouth to scream, but no sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:18.720
comes out. She reaches her ghostly fingers out&nbsp;
to brush your cheek, and everything goes black.

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:23.760
Doesn't that sound like a one-of-a-kind&nbsp;
experience? Don't be scared, that was no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:29.640
malicious spirit, it was just the lady of the&nbsp;
house! Clara Rosyth may not be the best hostess,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:34.440
but her home is lovely, a stately mansion&nbsp;
located in Dark Peak in Derbyshire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:39.720
England. Sure, it's a little haunted. But&nbsp;
all of the best historical houses are.

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:43.320
Daphne, 42, from London, had&nbsp;
this to say about her stay there:

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:47.880
"So cold...so cold...Check the children,&nbsp;
please? You have to check the children!"

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:52.920
Settle down, Daphne. Go back&nbsp;
to bed. Now, where was I?

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:57.300
Now maybe you don't want to be confined to&nbsp;
the space within the walls of a haunted house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.300 --> 00:14:02.220
or any house, for that matter. So how about&nbsp;
we get back to nature with a nice, simple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:06.480
lakeside camping trip? Just set up your&nbsp;
tent at least 50 meters away from the water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:11.520
and take in the crisp fresh air and wonderful&nbsp;
view. Feel the breeze rolling in off of the lake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:16.140
and...oh what's that? Do you see something,&nbsp;
floating in the water? It's alright,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:21.660
it's just SCP-2316. If you look for a&nbsp;
while, it might start to look familiar.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:22.980
Right, Chris from Iowa?

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:27.720
"I recognize them. The bodies,&nbsp;
in the water. I know them. My&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.720
friends...I'm so sorry. I have&nbsp;
to go. I have to go to them..."

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:38.100
Alright, buddy, you do that. Anyway, if you&nbsp;
do decide to visit SCP-2316, try and remember:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:44.100
You do not recognize the bodies in the water. And&nbsp;
maybe don't take a dip in that particular lake.

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:48.420
You've heard about Christmas in December,&nbsp;
and even Christmas in July, but how would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:53.820
you like to visit a place where it's Christmas&nbsp;
all year round, and the holiday fun never stops?

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:59.760
If that sounds like heaven on earth to you, then&nbsp;
you'll be a perfect fit for SCP-784, Christmas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:04.680
Cheer. This quaint little neighborhood in Texas&nbsp;
doesn't have much to offer in terms of sights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:09.600
with only twenty-four houses and two apartment&nbsp;
buildings, but the atmosphere more than makes up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:14.340
for it. No matter what time of year you visit,&nbsp;
the town will always be covered in a layer of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:19.800
freshly fallen snow, and every building is wrapped&nbsp;
in Christmas lights at a density of fifteen lights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:24.900
per square meter. And if you thought the decor&nbsp;
was charming, wait until you meet the residents!

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:30.000
Every person in SCP-784 is dressed in&nbsp;
their Holiday best, usually in novelty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:34.740
Christmas sweaters emblazoned with smiling&nbsp;
reindeer, Santa Claus, glittering ornaments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:38.400
and twinkling lights, and really just&nbsp;
about anything that screams "Christmas!"

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:43.620
During the day, the townspeople will decorate&nbsp;
their houses and exchange presents, as well as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:48.120
putting on Christmas pageants and dances.&nbsp;
When night falls, they will share eggnog,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:53.100
sing Christmas carols, and decorate any foreign&nbsp;
objects that might have made their way into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:57.780
town's vicinity. Just make sure that you&nbsp;
keep your Christmas Spirit at its best and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.780 --> 00:16:01.620
brightest while you're visiting, or you might&nbsp;
find yourself tied up with string lights and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:06.480
dragged into the nearest house for a bit&nbsp;
of Yuletide Reprogramming. Whether you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:10.140
looking for a place to spend Christmas,&nbsp;
or just trying to inject a bit of extra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:16.740
festivity into your everyday life, this is&nbsp;
the perfect place for your ho ho holiday!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:19.620
Unfortunately, none of our&nbsp;
clients who've chosen this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.680
destination will stop singing carols&nbsp;
long enough to provide testimony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:28.440
but just take that as a sign that their time in&nbsp;
this Christmas Village was truly life-changing.

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:33.120
Do you consider yourself something of a bookworm?&nbsp;
When your friends are going out to private clubs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:36.360
enjoying gourmet dinners, or headed&nbsp;
on early morning hikes on the beach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:40.920
do you prefer to stay in and crack open&nbsp;
your favorite novel? Then perhaps you'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:47.160
like to visit the best library in any known&nbsp;
universe. That's right, a book-lover's fantasy.

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:52.380
The Wanderer's Library is an interdimensional&nbsp;
library that acts as the embodiment of all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:56.760
knowledge. Its ever-expanding collection of&nbsp;
literature includes every book ever written,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:56.760 --> 00:17:01.620
and some that haven't been written yet&nbsp;
in your native timeline! Wander the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:06.660
endless stacks of books, take in the peaceful&nbsp;
environment, and study up on any subject your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:11.160
heart desires. And if you're not prepared&nbsp;
to completely unplug, there's also wifi!

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:15.300
Professor Lisa Graham thoroughly enjoyed&nbsp;
her stay in the Wanderer's Library!

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:19.560
"I know a little bit of everything now.&nbsp;
I've looked into the past, the present,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.900
the future...the greatest minds in the multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:25.440
at my fingertips. How am I supposed to&nbsp;
go back to a 9 to 5 job after that?!"

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:30.268
Now, we've covered quite a few places under the&nbsp;
jurisdiction of the SCP Foundation, but our final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.268 --> 00:17:30.360
offering is something quite exceptional: the&nbsp;
chance to stay at an official Foundation site.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:35.700
The SCP Foundation's Site-19 is the perfect&nbsp;
getaway for a real Foundation enthusiast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:40.500
someone who's a massive fan of the work&nbsp;
they do and excited to see all of their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:44.880
favorite anomalies and scientists.&nbsp;
Meet the famous Dr. Jack Bright! Just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:48.900
don't touch that amulet. Say hello to&nbsp;
Dr. Gears before he shoos you away so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:53.760
he can focus on his work. And do you like&nbsp;
anomalies? They've got them in spades here!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:18:00.720
SCP-035, the Possessive Mask, glowers out from&nbsp;
its protective glass case. SCP-096 huddles in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:06.900
the corner of its containment cell, hiding its&nbsp;
face. No peeking! Maybe you'll get to see SCP-049&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:10.440
performing one of his trademark experiments,&nbsp;
though if you're feeling under the weather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:15.480
you might not want to let him see you.&nbsp;
Maybe you want to sneak a look at SCP-173,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:18.600
and see if you can catch it&nbsp;
snapping any D-Class necks!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:23.400
Feel something nudging your foot? It's&nbsp;
just the friendly instances of SCP-131,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:27.900
here to check things out and make sure you're&nbsp;
having a fantastic time. If you're tired,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:32.400
get some rest in the employee sleeping&nbsp;
quarters. Hungry? Grab a bite at the canteen.

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:35.580
There's just so much to do&nbsp;
here at Foundation Site-19-

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.080
"Hey, you're not authorized to be in here!"

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:39.600
Just giving a tour, gentlemen,&nbsp;
I'll be finished in a moment.

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:42.960
"Sir, I'm going to have to ask you to leave.&nbsp;
If you don't comply, I'll have to use force."

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:48.000
Looks like that's my cue! All payments can be made&nbsp;
out to Marshall, Carter, and Dark! Think of us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:54.300
when you book your next vacation! And remember:&nbsp;
Absolutely no refunds under any circumstances.

00:18:54.300 --> 00:19:02.220
Now go check out “SCP-2521 and Infohazard&nbsp;
SCPs Explained” and “SCP-002 The Living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:07.500
Room &amp; the Most Terrifying SCP Rooms”&nbsp;
for more malevolent SCP rundowns!

